{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23363 - PROTEIN:6325",
  "verbalization": "Br-Xanthone A appears to be a target of multiple entities that ultimately lead to the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase. The evidence suggests that Br-Xanthone A interacts with WM-115, which is a target of several compounds, including 1-Heptadecene, 4-Prop-2-Enoxychromen-2-One, and 19-Oxo-3-beta,5,14-trihydroxy-5-beta-bufa-20,22-dienolide-3-acetate. These compounds, in turn, are targets of the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase. This indicates a potential pathway where Br-Xanthone A may influence the activity of the helicase through its interaction with these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Br-Xanthone A could modulate the function of the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
